{"id":"h04t3","name":"Courier Shifts and Idle Time","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>deliveries</b> has the columns <code>delivery_id</code>, <code>courier_id</code>, <code>picked_at</code>, <code>dropped_at</code> (timestamps) and <code>cancelled</code> (boolean). Cancelled deliveries and deliveries with no <code>dropped_at</code> (lost parcels) are ignored everywhere.</p>\n<p>The deliveries of a courier are grouped into <b>shifts</b>. Sort the deliveries of a courier by <code>picked_at</code> (then <code>dropped_at</code>). A delivery starts a new shift when its <code>picked_at</code> is <b>more than 30 minutes</b> after the latest <code>dropped_at</code> seen so far for that courier; a gap of exactly 30 minutes stays in the same shift. Shifts are numbered 1, 2, 3... per courier in time order.</p>\n<p>A courier can carry several parcels at once, so deliveries can overlap. The <b>busy time</b> of a shift is the number of minutes during which the courier carried at least one parcel: overlapping minutes count once. The <b>idle percentage</b> is <code>100 * (shift length - busy time) / shift length</code>, where the shift length goes from the first <code>picked_at</code> to the last <code>dropped_at</code> of the shift. When the shift length is 0, the idle percentage is 0.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the columns <code>courier_id</code>, <code>shift_no</code>, <code>shift_start</code>, <code>shift_end</code>, <code>deliveries</code>, <code>busy_minutes</code> (integer) and <code>idle_pct</code> (rounded to 1 decimal), sorted by <code>courier_id</code>, then <code>shift_no</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>deliveries</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>delivery_id</th><th>courier_id</th><th>picked_at</th><th>dropped_at</th><th>cancelled</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>7</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>2026-03-02 08:20:00</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>7</td><td>2026-03-02 08:10:00</td><td>2026-03-02 08:35:00</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>7</td><td>2026-03-02 09:05:00</td><td>2026-03-02 09:20:00</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>7</td><td>2026-03-02 11:20:00</td><td>2026-03-02 11:50:00</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>7</td><td>2026-03-02 11:25:00</td><td>2026-03-02 11:35:00</td><td>true</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>7</td><td>2026-03-02 13:00:00</td><td>null</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>9</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>2026-03-02 10:00:00</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>9</td><td>2026-03-02 08:30:00</td><td>2026-03-02 08:40:00</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>9</td><td>2026-03-02 10:10:00</td><td>2026-03-02 10:20:00</td><td>false</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>courier_id</th><th>shift_no</th><th>shift_start</th><th>shift_end</th><th>deliveries</th><th>busy_minutes</th><th>idle_pct</th></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>2026-03-02 09:20:00</td><td>3</td><td>50</td><td>37.5</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02 11:20:00</td><td>2026-03-02 11:50:00</td><td>1</td><td>30</td><td>0.0</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>2026-03-02 10:20:00</td><td>3</td><td>130</td><td>7.1</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>deliveries</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>courier_id</code>, <code>shift_no</code>, <code>shift_start</code>, <code>shift_end</code>, <code>deliveries</code>, <code>busy_minutes</code>, <code>idle_pct</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["îlots à deux niveaux","MAX cumulé","intervalles qui se chevauchent","division"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>deliveries</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 7 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>courier_id</code>, <code>shift_no</code>, <code>shift_start</code>, <code>shift_end</code>, <code>deliveries</code>, <code>busy_minutes</code>, <code>idle_pct</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; les dates s'affichent AAAA-MM-JJ HH:MM:SS pour une date avec heure.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"deliveries":{"columns":[["delivery_id","INT"],["courier_id","INT"],["picked_at","TIMESTAMP"],["dropped_at","TIMESTAMP"],["cancelled","BOOLEAN"]],"rows":[[1,7,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","2026-03-02 08:20:00",false],[2,7,"2026-03-02 08:10:00","2026-03-02 08:35:00",false],[3,7,"2026-03-02 09:05:00","2026-03-02 09:20:00",false],[4,7,"2026-03-02 11:20:00","2026-03-02 11:50:00",false],[5,7,"2026-03-02 11:25:00","2026-03-02 11:35:00",true],[6,7,"2026-03-02 13:00:00",null,false],[7,9,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","2026-03-02 10:00:00",false],[8,9,"2026-03-02 08:30:00","2026-03-02 08:40:00",false],[9,9,"2026-03-02 10:10:00","2026-03-02 10:20:00",false]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["courier_id","shift_no","shift_start","shift_end","deliveries","busy_minutes","idle_pct"],"rows":[[7,1,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","2026-03-02 09:20:00",3,50,37.5],[7,2,"2026-03-02 11:20:00","2026-03-02 11:50:00",1,30,0.0],[9,1,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","2026-03-02 10:20:00",3,130,7.1]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"deliveries":{"columns":[["delivery_id","INT"],["courier_id","INT"],["picked_at","TIMESTAMP"],["dropped_at","TIMESTAMP"],["cancelled","BOOLEAN"]],"rows":[[1,3,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","2026-03-02 08:00:00",false],[2,3,"2026-03-02 09:30:00","2026-03-02 09:40:00",false],[3,3,"2026-03-02 10:10:00","2026-03-02 10:11:00",false],[4,4,"2026-03-02 08:10:00","2026-03-02 08:50:00",true]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["courier_id","shift_no","shift_start","shift_end","deliveries","busy_minutes","idle_pct"],"rows":[[3,1,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","2026-03-02 08:00:00",1,0,0.0],[3,2,"2026-03-02 09:30:00","2026-03-02 10:11:00",2,11,73.2]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}